00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.880
Fraser River or Burrard inlet should immediately confirm that hydraulic modeling, dispersion modeling,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:23.360
and sensitivity analyses still reflect maximum design flows rather than average or nominal rates.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.580
Practitioners should also verify that indigenous consultation records, species at risk act,

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.480
compliance documentation, and any associated adaptive management triggers remain current given

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.580
the elevated operational tempo that is now expected to persist through at least May.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:42.580
The practical takeaway is clear. Even in the absence of new regulatory amendments,

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:48.200
operational tempo alone can reopen foundational assumptions buried in older approvals and permits.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.020
In practice, this means pulling out your existence.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.820
G contingency plans and risk registers and rerunning the numbers at sustained maximum throughput

